### Approval chains API v1. Reads are anonymous; changes need an admin or super admin in the temporary X-Acting-User-Id header (1 = Super Admin).
### Select the "local" environment (http/http-client.env.json). Run requests top to bottom.
### Seeded: chain 1 is the default; department ids 3 Accounts, 4 QA, 5 Delivery.

### List chains (default first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains
Accept: application/json

### Get the default chain
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Accept: application/json

### Edit the default chain: ordered approving departments
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Acting-User-Id: 1

{
  "name": "Default",
  "description": "Company wide",
  "departmentIds": [3, 4, 5]
}

### Which chain does catalog 1000 follow? (own chain, else the default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/for-catalog/1000
Accept: application/json

### Give catalog 1000 its own chain (409 if it already has one)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains
Content-Type: application/json
X-Acting-User-Id: 1

{
  "name": "Premium bags",
  "catalogId": 1000,
  "departmentIds": [3, 4, 5]
}

### Delete the catalog chain (the catalog goes back to the default)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
X-Acting-User-Id: 1

### The default chain cannot be deleted (409)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
X-Acting-User-Id: 1

### Without an acting user changes return 401
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Default", "departmentIds": [4] }

### Unknown id returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-chains/999999
Accept: application/json
